

 **Handwritten Digit Recognition using Deep Learning**.

This application allows users to draw any handwritten digit (0–9) on an interactive canvas, and the model instantly predicts the digit with a confidence score and probability distribution for all classes.

### 💡 Project Highlights

✅ Interactive drawing canvas for handwritten digits
✅ Real-time digit prediction using a trained deep learning model
✅ Displays prediction confidence and class-wise probabilities
✅ Image preprocessing before inference for improved accuracy
✅ Simple, clean, and user-friendly web interface built with Streamlit

### 🛠️ Technologies Used

* 🐍 Python
* 🧠 TensorFlow / Keras
* 🌐 Streamlit
* 🖼️ Pillow (PIL)
* 🔢 NumPy

### ⚙️ How It Works

1️⃣ The user draws a digit on the canvas.
2️⃣ The drawing is converted to grayscale and resized to **28×28 pixels**.
3️⃣ Pixel values are normalized and inverted to match the training dataset format.
4️⃣ The processed image is passed to the trained deep learning model.
5️⃣ The model predicts the digit and displays:

* Predicted digit
* Confidence percentage
* Probability for each digit (0–9)



